-- title:
--   Lemma 5.7 — soundness of witnesses
-- statement:
--   Consider a game $G$ with a reward function $r$, a succinct discount factor $\lambda=1-2^{-2^{B_\lambda}}$ and additive error $\varepsilon=2^{-B_\varepsilon}$, and let $(\sigma,\tau,I_\sigma,I_\tau)$ be a witness. Then $(L_\sigma,U_\tau)$ is an $\varepsilon$-approximation of $\mathrm{val}_\lambda$:
--   $$\mathrm{val}_\lambda(s)\in[L_\sigma(s),U_\tau(s)]\quad\text{and}\quad U_\tau(s)-L_\sigma(s)\le\varepsilon\qquad\text{for all states }s.$$
--   Moreover, $\sigma$ and $\tau$ are $\varepsilon$-optimal for $\mathrm{Disc}(r,\lambda)$.
--
--   Soundness turns every accepted witness into an approximation of the values and into $\varepsilon$-optimal strategies.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite game G = (S, A, B, δ) with |S| = n and at most m actions per player → states Fin n, actions Fin mA and Fin mB with n, mA, mB ≥ 1, m = max(mA, mB), distributions as nonnegative real vectors summing to one; reason: relabelling of finite sets; nonempty state and action sets are the source game convention
--   - encoding: the probability measure on valid plays Ω_s generated by finite histories, strategies on valid histories → the Ionescu-Tulcea trajectory measure on all sequences in (S × A × B)^ℕ; strategies are defined on all finite stage lists; reason: invalid plays have probability zero and values of strategies on invalid histories never matter, so every expectation and value is unchanged
--   - generalization: a game whose rewards are rationals defined using at most B_inp bits (as in the definition of witnesses), ε = 2^{-Bε} → any real game and real reward function with values in [0,1]; any Bε ∈ ℕ₀; reason: soundness does not use rationality or ε < 1; the rational instances with Bε ≥ 1 are a special case
-- source:
--   Ali Asadi, Krishnendu Chatterjee, The Computational Complexity of Concurrent Stochastic Games: Exact Value and Approximation, STOC 2027 submission #285 (October 2026), SHA-256 5cff187cf6b230b3bdfe540f2832f824d1ddb6acb43239fbf469d37c43b0d461, https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/285.pdf, Lemma 5.7, printed p. 15 (PDF p. 17)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Game
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_PowerSeries
import Definitions.Def_ConcurrentStochasticApprox_Approx_Problems
open Finset

namespace ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx

/-- **Lemma 5.7 (Soundness of witnesses).** For a game `G` with reward function `r`, succinct
discount factor `λ = 1 - 2^{-2^{Bλ}}` and additive error `ε = 2^{-Bε}`, every witness
`(σ, τ, I_σ, I_τ)` satisfies `L_σ(s) ≤ val_λ(s) ≤ U_τ(s)` and `U_τ(s) - L_σ(s) ≤ ε` at every state,
and both `σ` and `τ` are `ε`-optimal. -/
theorem lemma_5_7 {n mA mB : ℕ} (G : CSG n mA mB) (r : Reward n mA mB) (hr : IsReward r)
    (Blam Bε : ℕ) (W : WitnessData n mA mB) (hW : IsWitness G r Blam Bε W) :
    (∀ s, psVal (W.Lσ s) ≤ discValue G r (succinct Blam) s ∧
      discValue G r (succinct Blam) s ≤ psVal (W.Uτ s) ∧
      psVal (W.Uτ s) - psVal (W.Lσ s) ≤ (1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ Bε) ∧
    ∀ (hσ : ∀ s, IsDist fun a => psVal (W.σ s a)) (hτ : ∀ s, IsDist fun b => psVal (W.τ s b)),
      IsEpsOptimal₁ G (discObj r (succinct Blam)) ((1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ Bε) ((W.σStat hσ).toStrategy mB) ∧
      IsEpsOptimal₂ G (discObj r (succinct Blam)) ((1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ Bε) ((W.τStat hτ).toStrategy mA) := by sorry

end ConcurrentStochasticApprox.Approx
